{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles","id":558540,"title":"Rworking the Kupala plot in Transylvania Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T12:32:20-07:00","id":558540,"title":"Rworking the Kupala plot in Transylvania Chronicles","content":"I'm pondering STing the Translyvania Chronicles, and was thinking about reworking the Kupala plot angle, to make the whole thing seem a bit less contrived. I haven't quite finished reading the books yet, but I wanted to get some ideas down and out for discussion before they went out of my head. This mostly involves my own slightly different take on the Baali, which is still evolving, so may not entirely make sense yet. One big meta assumption/change here is that Kupala is a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> Basically, I envision making the Baali ongoing antagonists for the Chronicles, what with their connections to the infernal. Destroying a Baali nest at Budapest and finding hints pointing towards the tablet in their rituals and such would be the starting point. Much of Octavio's stuff would be subsumed in here, to the point where he's dropped as a character. Anatole may be introduced earlier, but possibly not.<br /> <br /> After this point, the characters may or may not build Tihuta Castle - I never understood why a patron asks them to build it if all they wanted was the tablet, given that they do so many fetch-quests anyway. It feels like a convenient point to introduce Zelios more than anything else, who could, again, be eliminated in favour of various geomantic hints in places that the PCs are sent over the course of other storylines.<br /> <br /> I also want to straighten out why the Tremere are so involved - they seem incidental, but involved everywhere. I think the key to figuring this out is reworking Saulot, given his probable involvement with the Baali. I know that Saulot's diablerie is the first sign of Gehenna, but....<br /> <br /> Hang on...<br /> <br /> What if Saulot wants the end of the world all along, and is the one orchestrating it all through Tremere?<br /> <br /> The Baali were a failed experiment thanks to Moloch, and so he starts gain with the Tremere, through his willing diablerie, hence why it is the first sign of Gehenna. So while the Baali are the evil devil-worshipping things, Kupala trying to impart things through them (whether they're trying to summon it or keep it asleep is a question that needs an answer here), so they're kind of the salvation of the world, ironically. Their involvement is why all the signs of Gehenna point to/are linked to Kupala, which is the source of Anatole's confusion over the prophecy (that the signs point to Kupala rather than Gehenna). They also provide an easy potential source of the geomantic information without Zelios - potentially being able to leech Kupala from these points, or being directed their by it in order to defend the parts it knows are its weak spots.<br /> <br /> Given this, what other changes are needed to the structure of TC to join up the dots? Anything that I've missed? Apologies for all the thinking aloud!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:13:09-07:00","id":559947,"title":"","content":"The Baali were created before Saulot achieved Golconda. He went to the East twice. From what I can tell from reading source books the Baali were probably made after his first trip. Even then, Saulot didn't achieve Golconda until sometime after returning to the Second city the second time. <br /> <br /> Saulot is a nice vampire, sort off. He's totally out for Gehenna. He is a lead player in the Jyhad. He's not looking for the Apocalypse just total Evil vampire destruction. That would be 99.9% of all vampires. The only difference from the other Antediluvians is that he's willing to help those who seek the road to salvation. And he wishes to protect humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:54:23-07:00","id":559969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=559947#post559947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Baali were created before Saulot achieved Golconda. He went to the East twice. From what I can tell from reading source books the Baali were probably made after his first trip. Even then, Saulot didn't achieve Golconda until sometime after returning to the Second city the second time.<br /> <br /> Saulot is a nice vampire, sort off. He's totally out for Gehenna. He is a lead player in the Jyhad. He's not looking for the Apocalypse just total Evil vampire destruction. That would be 99.9% of all vampires. The only difference from the other Antediluvians is that he's willing to help those who seek the road to salvation. And he wishes to protect humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...errrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr.....I don't think this is entirely true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:04:40-07:00","id":560709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=559969#post559969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...errrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr.....I don't think this is entirely true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which part. <br /> <br /> The Salubrie clan book gives a pretty good account of Saulot's history. p. 24 tells of when he achieved Golconda. This is well after the initial Baali Wars. Some reading is needed prior to p. 24 to get the whole story.<br /> <br /> As for my impression of Saulot as good but evil its sort of an amalgamation of everything that's been written. Basically the Core Rulebooks and Lair of the Hidden (Inconnu adventure book); Baali and Salubrie clan book etc.... Its not the only interpretation but its the one I usually go with. Saulot is a master at the Jyhad. His goal is to save humanity from the evil of vampires and assist those who wish to find personal salvation. I think the scenarios in the Gehenna book supports that view. Really nice but dangerous to those who don't share his world view. Golconda certainly hasn't made him any less dangerous. <br /> <br /> Like I said, this is my general impression of the guy. Please share if you feel there are nuances I've missed or facts that might change my point of view. Always open to great ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:04:32-07:00","id":560919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles#post558540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After this point, the characters may or may not build Tihuta Castle - I never understood why a patron asks them to build it if all they wanted was the tablet, given that they do so many fetch-quests anyway. It feels like a convenient point to introduce Zelios more than anything else, who could, again, be eliminated in favour of various geomantic hints in places that the PCs are sent over the course of other storylines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as far as i remember, the patrons - Radu, the princes and the PCs sires - had <b>nothing</b> to do with the tablet, they were just using the PCs to pay Nova Arpad a favor owed? And in fact her reason to recover it was pure and simple pride, being quite unaware of the tablet's actual value?<br /> <br /> Building up Tihuta Castle was their objective and a pretty relevant one from a strategic/political point of view, it gets involved in a bunch of historical events, even though the &quot;game of thrones&quot; ain't what guides the tale unfolding in the 4 books. The discovery of the tablet and the actual value of the terrible secrets contained in it, is wholly <b>of the players</b>, much like the geomantic plot with Zelios...<br /> <br /> I would have to thoroughfully read the books to be sure, but you seem to be terribly mixing NPC and ST/story objectives here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-19-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:05:52-07:00","id":561190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=560919#post560919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, as far as i remember, the patrons - Radu, the princes and the PCs sires - had <b>nothing</b> to do with the tablet, they were just using the PCs to pay Nova Arpad a favor owed? And in fact her reason to recover it was pure and simple pride, being quite unaware of the tablet's actual value?<br /> <br /> <br /> I would have to thoroughfully read the books to be sure, but you seem to be terribly mixing NPC and ST/story objectives here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly. It's the ST-eye-view that confuses me - the castle has precisely zero ongoing relevance to the plot, so I don't get why it's used to kick things off. I'm not saying it shouldn't be built, just that, from a story perspective, it doens't need to be the PCs doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T19:41:31-07:00","id":561518,"title":"","content":"OFF TOPIC:<br /> <br /> I apologize if my post isn't about Kupala, but because we're talking about TC i'd like to ask your opinion about something: i can't remember exactly when this happens but the coterie is going to meet the &quot;last cappadocian&quot; (a 7/8th generation Spanish nun if i remember correctly) after a while. Now this is the problem: a player of mine is playing a cappadocian and as a GM i should give him a chance to survive. Manual says this isn't an easy thing because the nun attracts a small army composed by Tremere and Giovanni, but she owns a scroll (a discipline) whose power should let everyone she has ever met forget about her existence.<br /> <br /> Honestly i don't like this solution, so i was wondering if anyone has ever found an alternative &quot;survival trick&quot; for both of them (nun+cappadocian player).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6330-ormans","name":"Ormans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6330_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T21:20:00-07:00","id":561542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=561190#post561190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite possibly. It's the ST-eye-view that confuses me - the castle has precisely zero ongoing relevance to the plot, so I don't get why it's used to kick things off. I'm not saying it shouldn't be built, just that, from a story perspective, it doesn't need to be the PCs doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a story perspective it's obtaining the domain that gets them in contact with Zelios, what then connected them to the whole &quot;Kupala web&quot; plotline and at the same time their being forsaken due to the spurious motives of the Nova Arpad incident is what leads to identify with the anarchs and participate on the strike at the Tzimisce antediluvian. There are certainly other possibilities, but it is the one the authors went with.<br /> <br /> Also, one things to remember is that it is the first chapter of the Transyslvania <b>Chronicles</b> - so, even if it does not relate directly to other events of the story arc, it serves as a major starting point for an ST's own stories. A group of neonates receiving right of domain and the support to claim and the 215 years between that and the theft of Nova Arpad offers a pretty strong start/backdrop even without the other events/flashpoints (that on their own are more of a story arc than a chronicle). It's there, along with 3 pages of regional timeline (for those without Transylvania By Night or the then nonexistent wiki to access) exactly to offer the ST story fodder that goes beyond fetch-quest after fetch-quest, so to speak.<br /> <br /> About the Tremere, the first challenge is see is telling a story relating to the return of Saulot without speaking of the Tremere... Not saying it can't be done - TC has so much hooks to expand one might actually develop a whole other major story arc without them - but at the moment i have no suggestion beyond taking your time to read the books and mine ideas/hooks.<br /> <br /> Also, what's to say the tablet's tale is true? What has the title &quot;Bone Dragon&quot; to do with Salubri? Sounds like something more appropriate to the - equally close-mouthed, mystical and transcedence-obsessed - Cappadocians, who coincidentally possess a pretty similar discipline set. Wasn't there something about Saulot possessing a first brood, made before his travels to the East and gaining a 3rd eye in the old Player's Guide? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:08:54-07:00","id":561570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ormans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=561518#post561518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OFF TOPIC:<br /> <br /> and as a GM i should give him a chance to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? The player most likely knew going in to a Dark Ages game the fate that was to befall the Cappadocians. Why should this character escape the coming purge solely by GM fiat when the entire might of Clan Giovanni plus a Baali contingent is set against them? How many groups over the years have played through that chapter with ANOTHER last surviving Cappadocian? What's wrong with playing out a story of a member of a doomed bloodline coming to the end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T00:12:24-07:00","id":561649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ormans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=561518#post561518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">she owns a scroll (a discipline) whose power should let everyone she has ever met forget about her existence.<br /> <br /> Honestly i don't like this solution, so i was wondering if anyone has ever found an alternative &amp;quot;survival trick&amp;quot; for both of them (nun+cappadocian player).</div> </div> </div> </div>The scroll isn't a survival trick - it only triggers after the death of the caster. It was a way to ensure her knowledge didn't benefit the Giovanni after she was gone.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the points, Baaldam. I'll get back to them soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T01:04:07-07:00","id":561663,"title":"","content":"Let your players come up with a clever plan for how to pull the fat out of the fire, that's their job. The GM just comes up with situations to throw at them (or at least, that's how I do things in my own games). What you should do, though, is adapt the game in response to your players' actions and choices. Whole point of playing RPGs and all, and where the Transylvania Chronicles fall so very flat. They're probably the most railroady set of adventures I've ever read.<br /> <br /> Even if your players don't make any effort to change the situation to their favor (smuggling out Maria, calling in allies, waylaying &quot;guests&quot; from ever arriving at the party), though... you should at least roll dice for the Baali and Giovanni trying to kill Maria. As I remember, the book just says 'Maria wards off the demons with her True Faith, then Ambrogino or the lead Baali-dude kills her.' No dice involved or anything, despite the presumed presence of PCs trying to prevent that very thing from happening. That's just dumb. Have the NPCs roll Brawl or Melee against Maria as normal, and give your PCs a fair chance to take them out before they can take Maria out (re: by using actual game mechanics when you're playing out the scenario). Whether she lives or dies, abiding by the fall of the dice is always preferable to the GM arbitrarily declaring &quot;such and such happens, nothing players do can matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, that &quot;Last Cappadocian&quot; thing is BS. There's Japheth, Lazarus/the Capuchin, Drenis, Angelique, Lady Constancia/Unre, the other Harbingers of the Skulls... probably a few others I'm not remembering off the top of my head, all before the PC in your game. Granted, maybe those individuals don't exist or won't be appearing in your game, but you certainly shouldn't feel obligated for Maria to be the world's last Cappadocian because the book says so. White Wolf's other writers didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T01:22:09-07:00","id":561667,"title":"","content":"Isn't it hinted that Pochtli is a Premascine Cappadocian although his loyalties are to the Giovanni? That would seem to be one way to get a surviving character of the parent clan that's a bit more mundane than being trapped in the Underworld for centuries. Just kiss Augustus' ring and never get caught doing anything disloyal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:34:46-07:00","id":562706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=561667#post561667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it hinted that Pochtli is a Premascine Cappadocian although his loyalties are to the Giovanni? That would seem to be one way to get a surviving character of the parent clan that's a bit more mundane than being trapped in the Underworld for centuries. Just kiss Augustus' ring and never get caught doing anything disloyal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand an association with the Cappadocians or Harbingers of Skulls on account of his skeletal visage, but if there's any actual hint of such, it is in Revised, because what clanbook: giovanni says is that he was one of the first pre-columbian priests embraced into the Giovanni as the Pisanob family. Anyway, i would say it is a pretty improbable tie, as Cappadocius' diablerie happens about half a century before Columbus arrival in the Americas - at best he could be the <b>childe</b> of an actual Premascine, unless one considers him a few decades to centuries older than the books say <b>and</b> descended of some Cappadocian playing Leif Ericson... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:32:00-07:00","id":564440,"title":"","content":"The revised Clanbook brings up the question but doesn't really answer one way or the other. As you say, embrace by European Cappodocians of the Giovanni family is pretty unlikely, though I wouldn't rule out the possibility of him having been embraced prior to the 15th century by some unrecorded explorer and seeing the writing on the wall early enough to ally himself with the Giovanni rather than the older members of the clan. We know the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Baali made it to the Americas in Pre-Columbian times, so it's not too great a stretch to have the odd member of another clan do so as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:31:35-07:00","id":564776,"title":"","content":"I prefer to think of Saulot as the biggest bastard of them all.<br /> <br /> He made 2 castes of Salubri. The Healers and the warriors. Neither was exactly what he wanted. He WANTED to win the jyhad. The Salubri were not the answer, to noble and good, he abandoned them. I highly doubt he felt any remorse when the Tremere hunted them down.<br /> <br /> He made the Baali. To much evil for evil sake (insert heavy metal music here). He abandoned them after they failed to destroy the Salubri the first time.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it for millennium, he ALLOWED Tremere to diablorize him. In them he gained the perfect army and the means by which to control them. Tremere made the mistake of thinking it was all his idea and deluded enough to think he would win the battle of wills against a truly ancient monster. In the end Saulot gets Tremere's body, Tremere is cast out and possess Goratrix, after formulating a back up plan using the Tremere Anti-tribu, he regains a small measure of his powers.<br /> <br /> So that's how I see the whole story playing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T00:42:47-07:00","id":568916,"title":"","content":"Also, I've been thinking far too hard about this particular piece of prophecy:<br /> <br /> As the Father is Destroyed<br /> And the Prodigals Buried,<br /> And the Cousins Rotted Away<br /> <br /> One Angel Survives to hold the Last Light of her True Clan<br /> <br /> And when Darkness Falls<br /> And Blackness Snuffs Out the Angel's Light,<br /> So passes another Barrier<br /> And the Final Nights draw ever closer<br /> <br /> The books have this apply to the last Cappadocian, but my compass points were put askew when I took part in a game where it was the last Salubri. The &quot;Father&quot; is Saulot, the &quot;Prodigals&quot; are the Salubri Warrior line (who I seem to remember were interred in torpor in a vault in the Senai desert in the game I played before), and the Cousins are the Tremere Antitribu.<br /> <br /> Does this work as an alternative reading? I'm unsure why, but I always felt like the Cappadocians were an afterthought.<br /> <br /> Also, any suggestions on how to involve Zelios other than he turns up and just by magical coincidence needs to carve a rune where the characters are headed next? I have real difficulty in how to make him non-incidental but also part of the overarching plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:04:46-07:00","id":572766,"title":"","content":"It could work. With prophecy, (from the ST's PoV), there can be multiple possibilities. From the Clan Novels, one of Anatole's final secret prophecies is something like &quot;And the Angel will descend into the Darkness of the Dragon's Bowels&quot;, which could be worked into this and indicating that it both was not about the Cappadocians or the &quot;last Cappadocian&quot;. With the Samedi and the Harbingers, there really was no &quot;last Cappadocian&quot;, either.<br /> <br /> Swapping it to Saulot/Salubri might actually make a lot of sense within the TC, too, as it's possible that Saulot would have learned about Ley Lines and the Geometrical webs in the East.<br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind is that both the Baali and the Tremere connection to the Salubri/Saulot is just speculation, and in both cases, when measured against other facts, do not really hold up. Remember, it was the Tzimisce Blood that created the Tremere. The Salubri had nothing at all to do with it. It was, like the Baali, 99% misdirection, but also a retroactive reason to turn a Clan that was pretty much well liked and respected into one almost universally reviled. Even combined, the Baali, Tremere, and Giovanni (all detested and notorious at the time) would not have been able to pull that off with minor influence and he said, she said, not when the healers and warriors had already proven themselves over and over, not to mention being arguably far more useful.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the later events in the TC, the Ivory Tablets are only a translation, not the actual tablets, and there is a pretty significant chance that 1.) well the KotE are particularly biased against Saulot, 2.) there was a mistranslation (it does say he did it in 1 hour and had a lot of difficulty with many words), 3.) again, the entire thing was simply misdirection (why would Saulot write this down?), or 4.) it's 100% fake.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that the prophecy could be referring to Clan Tzimisce, with the Prodigals being the Old Clan, and the Cousins being the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T03:33:42-07:00","id":1553438,"title":"","content":"...and as a dog returns to his vomit, I just can't let this reworking idea go. I've made it a bit more coherent this time round, though. Actually put ideas to work fixing it overall.<br /> <br /> I've only completed up to the Convention of Thorns at this point, as many of the activities after that are more dependent on the player group. There are thoughts beyond this, but those are far less settled. Much of the whole thing is up in the air still.<br /> <br /> Several of the thoughts I've had have been inspired by the World of Dark Ages podcast, the Transylvania Chronicles Redux series on Chimerical Realms (<a href=\"https://chimericalrealm.blogspot.com/2016/04/the-complete-transylvania-chronicles.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://chimericalrealm.blogspot.com...hronicles.html</a>) and the Storytelling TC series on Vampire Storyteller (<a href=\"https://vampirestoryteller.wordpress.com/category/general-storytelling/storytelling-tc/\" target=\"_blank\">https://vampirestoryteller.wordpress...orytelling-tc/</a>). Most particularly, the point-by-point breakdown I've used is taken mostly from the Transylvania Chronicles Redux series.<br /> <br /> The main outline that I've come up with (finalised up to the Convention of Thorns at this point), are guided by the following principles:<ul><li>As &quot;stop Kupala&quot; is the closest we get to a real through-line for the Chronicles, I've tried to make the Kupala cultists more present as antagonists overall. This will vary from Tzimisce to Baali cultists, depending on the context or the allegiance of the PCs.</li> </ul><ul><li>As part of that, I've replaced Octavian with the trio of Kupala Tzimisce as noted in Vampire Storyteller, and removed Lucita as entirely superfluous to the actual plot. Maybe the trio are the main Kupala cultist drivers, and the Baali come in later? Not sure. Could almost do a switcheroo of Anatole with Lucita, to actually give the prophet a character beyond being the prophet.</li> </ul><ul><li>Do more foreshadowing. I've tried to bring in a little bit of Yorak, the Anarch Revolt etc as sideline things before their big plot event, so that players aren't totally blindsided by them.</li> </ul><ul><li>Stop the spectator syndrome. I've tried to make it so that players can always have a choice of options about what to do at any point, without having to do something. This has frequently made anarchs the agents provocateur so far, as a wild card.</li> </ul><ul><li>Dracula sucks, have less of him.</li> </ul><br /> The link to the spreadsheet I'm using for notes is here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/123iwIuHMH2qBYFsGFTrHxmzXa18BrdBB/edit?usp=drive_link&amp;ouid=115928195430517637315&amp;rtp\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/123iwIuHMH2qBYFsGFTrHxmzXa18BrdBB/edit?usp=drive_link&amp;ouid=115928195430517637315&amp;rtp of=true&amp;sd=true</a><br /> <br /> The tab with my restructured plot is the &quot;Revised Plot&quot; tab. Others are just me collecting my thoughts and laying out the existing structure in a fashion I can work with.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear any and all thoughts on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T06:40:42-07:00","id":1553439,"title":"","content":"I think that it's kind of hilarous they have Saulot embracing the Baali as some big revelation of why he's evil.<br /> <br /> Except Saulot embraced the Baali as a <b><u>punishment</u></b>.<br /> <br /> It's just the Baali completely missed the message.<br /> <br /> Like Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T11:40:55-07:00","id":1553488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553439#post1553439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's kind of hilarous they have Saulot embracing the Baali as some big revelation of why he's evil.<br /> <br /> Except Saulot embraced the Baali as a <b><u>punishment</u></b>.<br /> <br /> It's just the Baali completely missed the message.<br /> <br /> Like Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, just like Caine, &quot;punishing&quot; someone with immortality and supernatural power backfired tremendously.<br /> <br /> Well, depending on who you ask I suppose. At the very least Saulot isn't Old Testament God and might have cared a little about collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Embracing the Baali may not have been 100% Evil\u2122, but it <i>does</i> mark Saulot as arrogant enough to re-enact divine punishment, and either wildly uncaring or uncharacteristically incapable of foresight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T18:05:39-07:00","id":1553495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553488#post1553488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, just like Caine, &quot;punishing&quot; someone with immortality and supernatural power backfired tremendously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 4th generation demon worshipers are not a good idea, Tsu-Lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, depending on who you ask I suppose. At the very least Saulot isn't Old Testament God and might have cared a little about collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Embracing the Baali may not have been 100% Evil\u2122, but it <i>does</i> mark Saulot as arrogant enough to re-enact divine punishment, and either wildly uncaring or uncharacteristically incapable of foresight. </div> </div> </div>At least unlike the other Antedilluvians (Haqim and Abilsamard aside), he created the Warrior Caste to clean up his mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T01:01:55-07:00","id":1553507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ideon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553488#post1553488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, just like Caine, &quot;punishing&quot; someone with immortality and supernatural power backfired tremendously.<br /> <br /> Well, depending on who you ask I suppose. At the very least Saulot isn't Old Testament God and might have cared a little about collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Embracing the Baali may not have been 100% Evil\u2122, but it <i>does</i> mark Saulot as arrogant enough to re-enact divine punishment, and either wildly uncaring or uncharacteristically incapable of foresight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought immortality was to ensure Caine didn't just off himself and get away from the punishment. And I could be wrong, but didn't Caine discover his powers through the Crone rather than having them given to him?<br /> <br /> That said, punishments that relies on degree of thinking are probably going to fly right over the head of a guy like Caine. A divine smack over the head might have worked better.<br /> <br /> As for Saulot, remember that this was kind of early in his existence so he not have had many more mental dots than a regular human, been on some esoteric Road by that point or just been on a power trip as an Antediluvian. Still a very stupid move but there may have been explanations for it, if no excuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T01:21:45-07:00","id":1553508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553507#post1553507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought immortality was to ensure Caine didn't just off himself and get away from the punishment. And I could be wrong, but didn't Caine discover his powers through the Crone rather than having them given to him</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a very interesting part many tend to overlook<br /> Caine lived cursed alone for an &quot;eon&quot; before embraced his first childe (in theory) - Eon could be a very long time (fun fact, a mitochondrial DNA and fossil evidence indicates that modern humans originated in North Africa about 300,000 years ago. Since Caine is the first child of the first human pair, and if &quot;eon&quot; is to be interpreted as a really long time, then Caine could very well be close to 300,000 years old.)<br /> Caine complained a bit about his exile, telling God/Metatron/Michael he will be killed and so on.... so recived the <b>Mark of Caine</b><br /> The mark of Cain is God's promise to offer Cain divine protection from premature death with the stated purpose of preventing anyone from killing him. With an extra bonus of the seven fold curse<br /> <br /> <u><b>Caine never really died</b></u><br /> <br /> Then came the Curses of the Archangels<br /> <br /> Michael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> Raphael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth,you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always. Hide now for the Sun rises to take its wrath on you.&quot;<br /> Uriel cursed him: \u201eThen, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness! You will drink only blood. You will eat only ashes. You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on. You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Not even died, but cursed to live on: &quot;You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not God per see who cursed him (or depends, thrugh the Archangels God expressed his Will)<br /> <br /> And more importantly, not even not died, when he recieved the curses... was an immortal basically, livin in the darkness, eating ash and blood. But technically, in <i>theory totally capable to reproduce normally</i><br /> <br /> You almost got it right ,it was not the Crone but Lilith<br /> <br /> Lilith tired to help him to Awake, but not really worked, tho the Book of Nod tells us, after the experience with the Archangels, Caine becomes officially &quot;Awakened&quot;, possessing the following Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Dominate, Presence, Protean, Animalism, and Auspex. Caine then became aware of the Path of Blood, the Final Path from which all paths stem. And with all these powers, he breaks his bond with Lilith and leaves her.<br /> Or at least the (unreliable)narrator of the Book of Nod interpret Caine's powers as disciplines - but not stated those were really disciplines or not<br /> Just Caine had powers<br /> <br /> &quot; I discovered how to move like lightning&quot;<br /> &quot;How to borrow the strength of the earth&quot;<br /> &quot;how to be as stone&quot;<br /> &quot;Lilith then showed me how she hides herself from hunters &quot;<br /> &quot;how she commands obedience&quot;<br /> &quot;and how she demands respect&quot;<br /> &quot; I found the way to alter forms&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to have dominion over animals&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to make eyes see sight&quot;<br /> (And more and more likely his powers were more on the Mage side, altering reality, hence the Curses he gleefully handed out...)<br /> <br /> Here comes the interesting part<br /> The Embrace<br /> Now immagine you are a Fledgeling Caitiff, no idea what the hell you are, what are you capable of and so on<br /> No established madia, works of fictions and so on around, so no Dracula, no vampire mtyhs, nothing<br /> How would you figure out how to Embrace?<br /> Realistically, no way you will ever kill someone, drain her dry and feed it with your blood...<br /> <br /> I think, at this is only my two cent in the matter only, when Caine after an eon handed out the first Embrace to spread his Curse... it was indeed a <i>curse</i><br /> Or an attempt to give eternal life<br /> A blood ritual, fuelled by his powers<br /> <br /> Why do I belive this?<br /> Book of Nod gives us the answer:<br /> <br /> &quot;But Caine grew lonely in his power.<br /> Deep within him the seed of loneliness blossomed, and grew a dark flower<br /> He saw within his blood the potence of fertility<br /> By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caine was the first Infernalist - well not counting Lilith herself of course who had her fair share of deal of Demons and called Mother of Monsters and Demons for a reason.... (and had an affair with Lucifer and had a bunch of Nephilim kids)<br /> <br /> So, the Embrace itself basically a blood ritual devised by Demons or at least they gave the idea for Caine how to do it - kill someone, rob him of the deserved afterlife and peace, and with his mighty blood, command and trap the soul in the dead body...<br /> <br /> In any case, tragic and fool are two expressions going hand in hand when we are talking about Caine<br /> An old pridefull fool, who is literally cursed to fail in everything he tries<br /> And even then, he could have stopped<br /> Uriel warned him:<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine, though powerful you are, and marked of God, know you this: that any Childe you make will bear your curse, that any of your Progeny will forever walk in the Land of Nod, and fear flame and sun, drinking blood only and eating ashes only. And since they will carry their father's jealous seed, they will forever plot and fight amongst themselves. Doom not those of Adam's grandchildren who seek to walk in righteousness. Caine! Stay your dread Embrace!&quot;<br /> <br /> But he decided to went along anyway\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T06:21:39-07:00","id":1553510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553508#post1553508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually a very interesting part many tend to overlook<br /> Caine lived cursed alone for an &quot;eon&quot; before embraced his first childe (in theory) - Eon could be a very long time (fun fact, a mitochondrial DNA and fossil evidence indicates that modern humans originated in North Africa about 300,000 years ago. Since Caine is the first child of the first human pair, and if &quot;eon&quot; is to be interpreted as a really long time, then Caine could very well be close to 300,000 years old.)<br /> Caine complained a bit about his exile, telling God/Metatron/Michael he will be killed and so on.... so recived the <b>Mark of Caine</b><br /> The mark of Cain is God's promise to offer Cain divine protection from premature death with the stated purpose of preventing anyone from killing him. With an extra bonus of the seven fold curse<br /> <br /> <u><b>Caine never really died</b></u><br /> <br /> Then came the Curses of the Archangels<br /> <br /> Michael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> Raphael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth,you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always. Hide now for the Sun rises to take its wrath on you.&quot;<br /> Uriel cursed him: \u201eThen, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness! You will drink only blood. You will eat only ashes. You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on. You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Not even died, but cursed to live on: &quot;You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not God per see who cursed him (or depends, thrugh the Archangels God expressed his Will)<br /> <br /> And more importantly, not even not died, when he recieved the curses... was an immortal basically, livin in the darkness, eating ash and blood. But technically, in <i>theory totally capable to reproduce normally</i><br /> <br /> You almost got it right ,it was not the Crone but Lilith<br /> <br /> Lilith tired to help him to Awake, but not really worked, tho the Book of Nod tells us, after the experience with the Archangels, Caine becomes officially &quot;Awakened&quot;, possessing the following Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Dominate, Presence, Protean, Animalism, and Auspex. Caine then became aware of the Path of Blood, the Final Path from which all paths stem. And with all these powers, he breaks his bond with Lilith and leaves her.<br /> Or at least the (unreliable)narrator of the Book of Nod interpret Caine's powers as disciplines - but not stated those were really disciplines or not<br /> Just Caine had powers<br /> <br /> &quot; I discovered how to move like lightning&quot;<br /> &quot;How to borrow the strength of the earth&quot;<br /> &quot;how to be as stone&quot;<br /> &quot;Lilith then showed me how she hides herself from hunters &quot;<br /> &quot;how she commands obedience&quot;<br /> &quot;and how she demands respect&quot;<br /> &quot; I found the way to alter forms&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to have dominion over animals&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to make eyes see sight&quot;<br /> (And more and more likely his powers were more on the Mage side, altering reality, hence the Curses he gleefully handed out...)<br /> <br /> Here comes the interesting part<br /> The Embrace<br /> Now immagine you are a Fledgeling Caitiff, no idea what the hell you are, what are you capable of and so on<br /> No established madia, works of fictions and so on around, so no Dracula, no vampire mtyhs, nothing<br /> How would you figure out how to Embrace?<br /> Realistically, no way you will ever kill someone, drain her dry and feed it with your blood...<br /> <br /> I think, at this is only my two cent in the matter only, when Caine after an eon handed out the first Embrace to spread his Curse... it was indeed a <i>curse</i><br /> Or an attempt to give eternal life<br /> A blood ritual, fuelled by his powers<br /> <br /> Why do I belive this?<br /> Book of Nod gives us the answer:<br /> <br /> &quot;But Caine grew lonely in his power.<br /> Deep within him the seed of loneliness blossomed, and grew a dark flower<br /> He saw within his blood the potence of fertility<br /> By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caine was the first Infernalist - well not counting Lilith herself of course who had her fair share of deal of Demons and called Mother of Monsters and Demons for a reason.... (and had an affair with Lucifer and had a bunch of Nephilim kids)<br /> <br /> So, the Embrace itself basically a blood ritual devised by Demons or at least they gave the idea for Caine how to do it - kill someone, rob him of the deserved afterlife and peace, and with his mighty blood, command and trap the soul in the dead body...<br /> <br /> In any case, tragic and fool are two expressions going hand in hand when we are talking about Caine<br /> An old pridefull fool, who is literally cursed to fail in everything he tries<br /> And even then, he could have stopped<br /> Uriel warned him:<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine, though powerful you are, and marked of God, know you this: that any Childe you make will bear your curse, that any of your Progeny will forever walk in the Land of Nod, and fear flame and sun, drinking blood only and eating ashes only. And since they will carry their father's jealous seed, they will forever plot and fight amongst themselves. Doom not those of Adam's grandchildren who seek to walk in righteousness. Caine! Stay your dread Embrace!&quot;<br /> <br /> But he decided to went along anyway\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Two observations:<br /> 1) the last words from Uriel regarding not dooming those who seek to walk in righteousness should entail some protection for those vampires who indeed wanted that. Sure, they bear the curses and the jealous seed - something that sadly does not get enough mechanical representation in the game, despite how central it is to vampire existence in the lore -, but they have fundamentally been wronged and should get some slack for that. It would be interesting to emphasise Golconda and redemption more - also mechanically - to explore this aspect further. It's obviously there in the lore and behind the Roads and Paths, but I'm seeing as even more important now, even if it only really applies to a small percentage of righteous humans who got stuck with vampirism;<br /> 2) I remember that in Demons the Fallen the Underworld was made by the demons because they didn't know where humans went after death and feared it for them, so the Underworld became a place to keep their souls instead of letting them move on. The idea of demons using Caine to give humans another way to stay in the world sounds pretty in line with that perspective. Also, wasn't there some plot thing about the first children of Caine educating mankind and ending up being killed due to some interference by the demons? I can't recall the details, but it sounds interesting to bring into the discussion;<br /> 3) the weird thing about the Embrace is that there is no real good in it for anyone: it's not good for humans who try to walk in righteousness, and it's also not good as punishment for the wicked, because they just get to be more powerful, wicked and a more enduring blight upon the world. It's pure selfishness from the one who does the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T07:43:21-07:00","id":1553513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/558540-rworking-the-kupala-plot-in-transylvania-chronicles?p=1553510#post1553510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) I remember that in Demons the Fallen the Underworld was made by the demons because they didn't know where humans went after death and feared it for them, so the Underworld became a place to keep their souls instead of letting them move on. The idea of demons using Caine to give humans another way to stay in the world sounds pretty in line with that perspective. Also, wasn't there some plot thing about the first children of Caine educating mankind and ending up being killed due to some interference by the demons? I can't recall the details, but it sounds interesting to bring into the discussion;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the book of nod, but spread over in several<br /> In<b> Revelations of the Dark Mother </b>Lilith describes <b>the Watchers</b> (fallen angels, essentially demons) who come to earth and teach forbidden secrets to mortals.<br /> These Watchers stir strife between humanity and Caine\u2019s children, playing on human fear and envy.<br /> The text implies that Caine\u2019s children were betrayed and destroyed because of whispers from these dark beings.<br /> <br /> Now in Demon the Fallen during the Time of Babel, Lucifer selected ten of his most trusted retainers and sent them across the land.<br /> <b>Girieal </b>taught the race of dust the secrets of the earth, how to shape the land through the art of combining elements and minerals.<br /> <b>Sharaael </b>imparted the knowledge of flesh and life so that mortals could recapture the immortality that God wrongly took away.<br /> <b>Bephamael</b> taught the race of mortals of the secrets of the stars and the heavens above. The <i>Book of Bephamael</i> traced the patterns of the stars and how to predict the passage of time.<br /> <b>Marael</b> taught them the secrets of wind and storm<br /> <b>Gamael</b> revealed the secret of metal work and the forge<br /> <b>Ur-Shanbi</b> taught mortals of fate and how to divine the future by looking at signs and portents<br /> <b>Samael</b> taught mortals where to look for the Mother of the Moon (Luna), what secrets she possessed and how to protect themselves from her kin (the Fera) - a little tangent here, but I alwas found it amusing there was the Civilization of the Mokol\u00e9 before the Humans, so maybe there were... Mokol\u00e9 Sebettu/Elohim too? Anyhow just fun to think about it<br /> <b>Agriel</b> wrote of the many secrets of the bounty of the land, of fruits both good and bad, and how to manipulate them for nourishment or poison.<br /> <b>Shamshiel </b>spoke to the race of Adam and Eve of the sun, God's unrelenting eye<br /> <b>Penemue </b>taught the race of man the gift of writing language and the wisdom this entails. Through his gift, mortals gained the ability to define the world according to symbols and concepts and not by <i>things</i> that needed to be seen or touched. The secrets he taught allowed mortals to open their own eyes. Creation no longer needed to be seen and touched to be believed. Knowledge could now spread of its own accord.<br /> <br /> It make sense, the Ten - who were Demons/Sebettu or at least Fallen Elohim back then - warned the Humans and even urged them to weed out Caine's line who single handedly was responsible for the Age of Wrath and Lucifer and the Ten probably were not really fond of him or his descendants (actually not just protectors of Humans like Lucifer, but even the cruel and &quot;evil&quot; Iron Legion and Silver Legion who commited atrocities were not really keen about the idea their subject humans rightfully Thiers were prayed upon by these strange cursed parasites)<br /> The Ten - ironically - were killed by the Nephilim<br /> In retaliation, Lucifer and his followers hunted them down and killed them (Azrael was the only one not involved with the creation of the Nephilim to discover their origin. He traded his silence, and the aid of the Alabaster Legion in rebellion against Lucifer, for the right to their souls when they finally passed on. These dead Nephilim worked as ferrymen in Haven, a job which was made easier due to their dual nature. What has happened to these dead Nephilim is unknown)<br /> Now It is unknown if any Nephilim survived to pass on their lineage to the Final Nights, but some folk are said to be the offspring of demons. Considering the carnal traffic at Sabbats, orgies and midnight visitations, this isn\u2019t surprising. Uncannily long-lived, impervious to pain, and often possessed of inhuman powers, a demon-spawn (or laham) is said to be a special servant of Hell and they are granted a special place at the tables of Npehandi and other primal diabolists, who can sense her demonic heritage.<br /> (Mechanically, player characters who take Laham Merit in Infernalism: The Path of Screams must also take the 4th level in the Echos Flaw as aswell. However, in M20's The Book of Secrets, the Echos Flaw drops to the 3rd level, suggesting a decrease in the vigilance of most Sleepers.)<br /> <br /> It is more ironic, Lucifer not really had problem to sire Nephilims of his own, with Lilith... but when others did it and killed his Watchers and ruined his plans he got angry and vengefull.<br /> <br /> <b>In Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat (1999, Revised)</b> the quasi-meta-narrative of the Sabbat beliefs and the hidden metaplot talks about how Noddist prophecies may conceal truths planted by other forces, including infernal powers and there\u2019s a strong hint that the Antediluvians themselves may have been manipulated by demons, particularly during the time after Caine\u2019s withdrawal.<br /> <br /> This was in a sense confirmed later when <b>Chaining the Beast</b> ment